00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.380
and the Marine Corps and other branches

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.790
have been working really hard

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.190
at taking hazing out of the equation.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:04.050
- Have you ever ordered a code red?

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:05.223
- I have never,

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:08.880
I mean I've done-

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.620
- Have you ordered a code red?

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:11.921
- I did what was required of me.

00:10:11.921 --> 00:10:13.290
- Have you ever ordered a code red?

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:15.013
- You're goddamn right I did.

00:10:15.013 --> 00:10:16.993
(Devin laughing)

00:10:16.993 --> 00:10:19.657
- Lieutenant Kendrick,
may I call you John?

00:10:19.657 --> 00:10:21.948
- No, you may not.

00:10:21.948 --> 00:10:23.920
- Have I done something to offend you?

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:25.945
- No, I like all you Navy boys.

00:10:25.945 --> 00:10:28.620
Every time we gotta go someplace to fight,

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.660
you fellas always give us a ride.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:32.280
- Well that's a pretty classic one,

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.720
well done to the script writer.

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:37.022
The U.S. Navy, the U.S.
Marine Corps taxi service.

00:10:37.022 --> 00:10:37.860
(Devin laughing)

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.630
- There was a platoon
meeting on September 6th

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.340
at four in the afternoon.

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:43.800
Lieutenant Kendrick says that
he gave strict instructions

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.050
that nothing was to happen to Santiago.

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.250
- Ma'am, that's correct.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.510
- And what happened then?

00:10:48.510 --> 00:10:50.670
- Lieutenant Kendrick
came to our room, ma'am.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:54.333
Lieutenant Kendrick ordered us
to give Santiago a code red.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.050
- Okay, so the way that they're
describing a code red here

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.352
sounds super illegal.

00:11:00.352 --> 00:11:01.185
It sounds like hazing,

00:11:01.185 --> 00:11:02.250
and I assume there are rules against that.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:03.102
Are Marines required to
follow illegal orders,

00:11:03.102 --> 00:11:08.102
assuming that that is an illegal order?

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.110
- No.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.420
So this is where it becomes complicated.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.580
The reality is it's a defense to say

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:16.050
I was ordered to do something,

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.820
but there are exceptions

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.310
and the exception is it's not a defense

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:23.190
if you either know that
the order is unlawful,

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:25.470
or a person of ordinary sense

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:27.030
and understanding would have known

00:11:27.030 --> 00:11:28.320
the orders to be unlawful.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.210
And now to be clear it's not a person,

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.980
you're not grabbing
someone off the street,

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:34.110
it's someone in that culture,

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.270
a Marine, a solider, what have you.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:39.120
- You're not permitted to question orders.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:40.800
- Then what's the secret, huh?

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.240
What are the magic words?

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.230
I give orders every day,

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.262
nobody follows them.

00:11:44.262 --> 00:11:45.750
- We have softball games
and marching bands,

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:48.150
they work at a place where
you have to wear camouflage

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.590
or you might get shot.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:51.060
- By the Cubans?

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:51.973
- Yeah.

00:11:51.973 --> 00:11:56.610
- I need you, you're better
at research than I am,

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:58.972
and you know how to prepare a witness.

00:11:58.972 --> 00:12:00.960
- I mean any law student should know

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.400
how to do legal research,

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:03.690
and any trial lawyer should know

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:04.890
how to prep a witness.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.410
- What is he really saying
that his strengths are?

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.243
I mean what is he saying?

00:12:08.243 --> 00:12:09.291
- Talking good.

00:12:09.291 --> 00:12:10.124
He can talk good.

00:12:10.124 --> 00:12:10.957
- His strengths are talking good.

00:12:10.957 --> 00:12:12.570
I don't really know what his
strengths are at this point,

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.010
except that he's Tom Cruise.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:16.680
- [Devin] Well that is a big plus there.

00:12:16.680 --> 00:12:17.730
- This is our defense.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:18.563
Intent.

00:12:18.563 --> 00:12:20.070
No one can prove there
was poison on the rag.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:21.630
Code red, they're common

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.070
and accepted in Guantanamo Bay.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:23.903
The order.

00:12:23.903 --> 00:12:24.736
A, Kendrick gave it,

00:12:24.736 --> 00:12:27.570
b, they had no choice but to follow it.

00:12:27.570 --> 00:12:29.280
- They're creating a theme

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:30.510
of their defense.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.790
They have three different holes

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.040
that they're trying to poke
in the prosecution's case,

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.770
and they're taking deeper dives

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.060
into the strategy of each one

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.370
so that they can fold that
into the rest of the trial.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.660
It's not terrible.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:43.493
- Right.

00:12:43.493 --> 00:12:46.890
And the reality is if they're only charged

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.150
with pre-meditated murder,

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:49.410
and that's the only theory

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:52.110
that the government is
going with on this one,

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.730
then focusing on that intent

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:55.470
could be a home run.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:57.300
They might be winning on that one.

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.880
Depending of course on
lesser included offenses

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.220
like unpremeditated
murder and man slaughter

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:03.510
and what have you.

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:05.010
But then focusing on the code red

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.840
and the order is also really important

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.730
exactly for that reason

00:13:08.730 --> 00:13:11.850
that following orders can
sometimes be a defense.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.980
And if they can say code
reds are super common

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:15.660
down in Guantanamo Bay,

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:18.330
then they may be able to say they thought

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:19.350
it was a legal order.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:21.210
And any ordinary person down there

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:22.350
would have thought it was legal.

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:23.400
- I've been trying to track down

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.500
a Lieutenant Colonel
Matthew Andrew Markinson.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.900
- Doctor, was there any
sign of external damage?

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:28.733
- [Doctor] No.

00:13:28.733 --> 00:13:29.877
- No scrapes?
- [Doctors] No.

00:13:29.877 --> 00:13:31.043
- No cuts?
- [Doctor] No.

00:13:31.043 --> 00:13:32.670
- Bruises, broken, bones?

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:33.750
- [Doctors] No.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.700
- Doctor, was there any sign of violence?

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:37.620
- You mean other than the dead body?

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:39.930
- Shit, walk into that every goddamn time.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:43.320
- So I think this is not
bad cross examination prep,

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.810
and it's something that
a lot of lawyers forego.

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:48.270
You gotta red team your own cases

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.260
and your own witnesses.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:51.510
And this is prepping for
the cross examination

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.880
of the doctor who's going
to be a hostile witness,

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:54.960
and who doesn't want you to be able

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.850
to poke holes in his medical opinion

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.970
regardless of whether he
thinks they're innocent or not.

00:13:59.970 --> 00:14:02.580
And you can't ask these kind of questions

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:04.830
that just set you up for a softball

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:08.280
for a hostile witness
to just jump all over.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.840
- The accused entered the barracks room

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:13.110
of their platoon mate
PFC William Santiago.

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:14.850
They woke him up, tied his arms

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:15.990
and legs with tape,

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:18.690
forced a rag into his throat.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.430
A few minutes later a chemical reaction

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:23.040
called lactic acidosis caused his lungs

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:24.570
to begin bleeding.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:25.920
He drowned in this own blood,

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.090
and was pronounced dead

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:29.781
at 37 minutes past midnight.

00:14:29.781 --> 00:14:32.055
These are the facts of the case,

00:14:32.055 --> 00:14:34.440
and they are undisputed.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:36.360
- All right, so

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:39.120
maybe a slightly argumentative
opening statement,

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.280
but he is talking about the things

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:44.880
that he is going to prove
in the course of this trial,

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:47.190
talking about what witnesses
are going to testify to.

00:14:47.190 --> 00:14:48.790
And highlighting the fact

00:14:49.639 --> 00:14:50.472
that a lot of these facts

00:14:50.472 --> 00:14:52.170
are not disputed by either side.

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.240
So some of this stuff
is gonna be a slam dunk.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.670
And I like that he's
actually using the lectern

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:57.840
that is between council table,

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.480
which is generally where you would be

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:01.680
giving these kinds of things,

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:03.390
not running all over the courtroom,

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:04.650
in the well in front of the jury,

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:06.330
and all that kind of stuff.

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:07.890
- That's right.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:09.240
The story I just told you-

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:11.940
- And of course now he's
in the well of the court

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:12.900
without permission.

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:14.160
- It's the exact same story

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.380
you're gonna hear from Private Downey.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.080
Now Lieutenant Kaffee is gonna try

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.060
and pull off a little magic act here.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:23.238
- And this is where it
starts going off the rails.

00:15:23.238 --> 00:15:24.960
When you start talking about

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:26.190
what the defense is gonna do,

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.320
and start talking about magic acts

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:29.790
and things like that,

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:31.650
you're losing it because you're no longer

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:33.180
focusing on what you're gonna do,

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:34.170
what you're gonna prove,

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:35.250
and how you're gonna prove this

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:37.080
beyond a reasonable doubt.

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:40.170
Now you're just playing into
the defenses hands essentially.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.880
And when we get to the end,

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.440
all the magic in the world

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.430
will not have been able

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:45.540
to divert your attention

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:48.393
from the fact that Willy Santiago is dead,

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:51.930
and Dawson and Downey killed him.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.190
- You can get close to the jury,

00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:54.330
if that's really what you wanna do,

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.700
but invading their personal space,

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.190
especially when, as
Kevin Bacon's character

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:00.240
is just a captain,

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:01.800
I saw on that panel

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:02.987
that there are people who outrank him,

00:16:02.987 --> 00:16:05.340
and do you really wanna
start getting close to them,

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:06.900
sharing their breathing space,

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.250
spittle coming out of your mouth,

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.083
and hitting them?

00:16:09.083 --> 00:16:09.916
No, you don't.

00:16:09.916 --> 00:16:11.190
Give them some breathing room,

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:12.111
be the professional,

00:16:12.111 --> 00:16:13.323
and don't do that.

00:16:14.702 --> 00:16:15.797
- Lieutenant Kaffee.

00:16:15.797 --> 00:16:17.310
- There was no poison on the rag.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.410
- Stand up, dude. (laughing)

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.820
- Prove otherwise is futile,

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:22.120
'cause it just ain't true.

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:26.936
When Dawson and Downey went
into Santiago's room that night-

00:16:26.936 --> 00:16:29.580
- No, stand, no, no, stop walking.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.627
- It wasn't to kill or harm,

00:16:30.627 --> 00:16:32.670
and it wasn't because they
were looking for kicks

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.503
on a Friday night,

00:16:33.503 --> 00:16:36.180
it's because it was what
they were ordered to do.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:37.800
Now, out in the real
world that means nothing,

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.658
and here at the Washington Navy Yard

00:16:39.658 --> 00:16:42.510
it doesn't mean a whole lot more.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:44.850
But if you're a Marine assigned to

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:48.307
Rifle Security Company
Windward, Guantanamo Bay, Cuba,

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:50.490
you're given an order you follow it

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.840
or you pack your bags.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.640
- The most condescending
thing you could say

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:57.360
oh, following orders doesn't
matter in the United States,

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:01.080
but it does when you're in
Guantanamo Bay in peace time.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.300
- Right, because remember the
Marines down in Guantanamo

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:05.460
are fanatical, notoriously so.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.770
Tom Cruise's character is a Navy officer,

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:10.230
and he's speaking in a way that perhaps

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:12.120
Navy officers would,

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.120
but remember on that panel are
a bunch of Marines as well,

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.010
and they're probably
listening to this thinking

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:19.920
this guy has no idea what
the hell he's talking about.

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.470
- Commander, is it possible for a person

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:24.289
to have an affliction,
some sort of condition

00:17:24.289 --> 00:17:28.110
which might also speed up
the process of acidosis?

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.250
- It's possible.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:31.410
There would still be symptoms though.

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:33.150
- What kind of symptoms?

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:33.983
- There are hundreds of-

00:17:33.983 --> 00:17:35.151
- [Danny] Chest pains?

00:17:35.151 --> 00:17:36.060
- Yes.

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:37.320
- Shortness of breath?

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:38.153
- [Doctor] Yes.

00:17:38.153 --> 00:17:39.150
- Fatigue?

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:40.710
- Of crouse.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.360
- Doctor, is this your signature?

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:45.060
- Yes it is.

00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:46.560
- Would you read your handwritten remarks

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:48.293
at the bottom of the page, please, sir?

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:51.300
- Initial testing negative,

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.340
patient complains of chest pains,

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.320
shortness of breath and fatigue.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:59.430
- Getting that witness to
say exactly what he said

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:01.380
at some previous time

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:02.310
is perfect.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:05.160
- In your professional medical opinion,

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.050
was Willy Santiago poisoned?

00:18:07.050 --> 00:18:08.550
- Your honor, we renew our objections

00:18:08.550 --> 00:18:09.810
to Commander Stone's testimony,

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:11.820
and ask that it be
stricken from the record.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:12.840
We further ask the court

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:13.770
to instruct the court members

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:16.838
to lend no weight to
this witnesses testimony.

00:18:16.838 --> 00:18:18.552
- The objection's overruled, council.

00:18:18.552 --> 00:18:20.370
- Your honor, the defense
strenuously objects

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:21.930
and requests an 802 conference

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:23.490
so that his honor might
have an opportunity

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:26.130
to hear discussion before
ruling on this objection.

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:28.470
- The objection of the
defense has been heard

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:29.700
and overruled.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:30.960
- Move to reconsider.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.490
- Your objection is noted,

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:33.870
the witness is an expert,

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.940
and the court will hear his opinion.

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:37.770
- You're not supposed
to object to everything.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.390
You can really seem like the jerk

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.670
when you're making this
long speaking objection

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:42.990
that's totally unnecessary,

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:45.240
and it's very clear she's not doing

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:46.800
what everybody else wants her to do

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:48.750
in this particular situation,

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:50.370
strenuously objecting.

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.410
- Oh wow, strenuously objecting,

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:53.910
I should take some time to reconsider.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:55.080
- Including the judge,

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:58.770
who, he's kept a pretty
tight lid on things,

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:01.080
but you do not want to get a judge

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:02.691
into that kind of behavior,

00:19:02.691 --> 00:19:04.860
it's only downhill from there.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:06.930
- Lieutenant, do you
know what a code red is?

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.190
- Yes, I do.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:09.720
- Have you ever ordered a code red?

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.370
- No, I have not.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.980
- I mean, so this is
what's really dangerous

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:16.860
about testifying under oath is that

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:18.240
that's probably not true.

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:19.410
He's probably ordered a bunch.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:23.610
I mean the prior Marine testified

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:25.740
that code reds were
happening all the time.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:27.720
I would call so many rebuttal witnesses

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:30.060
that are like yeah,
Kendrick told me to order

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:33.360
code red on this day and
this day and this day,

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.610
and just destroy his credibility.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:37.230
- An officer in his position,

00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:40.410
he may not be the one
directly ordering code reds

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:42.960
on kind of a day to day basis,

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:46.260
and so the people who are
probably pushing the code reds

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:49.680
in this film at least are the corporals,

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.150
the sergeants,

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:53.400
and maybe even some lance corporals.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:56.130
- Now we object to this
entire line of questioning.

00:19:56.130 --> 00:19:57.840
- The government's objection is sustained

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:58.830
Lieutenant Kaffee,

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:01.050
and I would remind you
that you're now questioning

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:03.870
a Marine officer with an
impeccable service record.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:05.760
- So what?

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:06.780
What?

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.790
Why would the judge make that comment?

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:10.380
That is commenting on the evidence

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:12.510
by actually explicitly talking about

00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:14.010
this guy's performance evaluations.

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:15.990
Also, how does this judge even know

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.270
this Lieutenant's performance evaluations?

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:21.570
There's nothing wrong with
asking pointed questions

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:22.950
of a Marine officer.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.630
I mean they're not gods.

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:26.040
- Can Dawson determine on his own

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:27.420
which orders he's going to follow?

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:28.860
- No, he cannot.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:32.010
- Why did you go to
Private Santiago's room

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:33.993
on the night of September 6th?

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:37.110
- A code red was ordered
by my platoon commander,

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:38.860
Lieutenant Jonathan James Kendrick.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:40.883
- Thank you.

00:20:40.883 --> 00:20:42.960
- Do Marines have a Fifth Amendment right

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.070
not to testify?

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:45.150
- Absolutely.

00:20:45.150 --> 00:20:48.570
You have the same right at a
trial, at a Court Marshall.

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:49.920
You do not have to take the stand,

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:51.168
you can if you want to.

00:20:51.168 --> 00:20:53.460
The panel members are
going to be instructed

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:55.830
exactly like a civilian criminal trial,

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.540
that he has a right to remain silent,

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:59.460
and you can't take into consideration

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:01.440
whether they choose not to testify.

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:04.260
- Did you ever actually
hear Lieutenant Kendrick

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:05.490
order a code red?

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.140
- Well, Hal said that-

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:09.870
- Private, did you ever actually hear

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.453
Lieutenant Kendrick order a code red?

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:14.785
- No, sir.

00:21:14.785 --> 00:21:15.725
- If it please the court,

00:21:15.725 --> 00:21:16.558
I'd like to request a recess

00:21:16.558 --> 00:21:17.640
in order to confer with my client.

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:19.260
- There's a couple things here.

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:20.190
This is a great example

00:21:20.190 --> 00:21:22.560
of why you shouldn't object

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:23.760
every time you can,

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:26.040
because it really puts
an exclamation point

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:28.320
on something happened that I didn't like.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:30.030
- As far as that private goes,

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:32.490
it actually strengthens his case,

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:34.440
but here's where it gets even worse.

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.762
Remember, this is a co-defendant trial.

00:21:36.762 --> 00:21:39.540
These two are on trial at the same time.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:40.740
- They're represented by the same-

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:43.391
- They're represented by
the same defense attorneys,

00:21:43.391 --> 00:21:47.867
and right now their interests
materially conflict.

00:21:47.867 --> 00:21:51.270
Also, let's talk about witness
preparation for a second.

00:21:51.270 --> 00:21:52.956
- You know how to prepare a witness.

00:21:52.956 --> 00:21:53.940
(Devin laughing)

00:21:53.940 --> 00:21:58.170
- The way in which this most
vital piece of information

00:21:58.170 --> 00:22:00.960
can get overlooked so that the first time

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:04.200
that we're hearing about
it is on cross examination.

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:07.964
That is a failure, an absolute failure.

00:22:07.964 --> 00:22:10.547
(upbeat music)

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:14.390
- How are you feeling?

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:20.282
- Well, I think Jessep's gonna
have his hands full today.

00:22:20.282 --> 00:22:22.770
(Danny laughing)

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:27.120
- Listen, Danny, when
you're out there today,

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:30.453
if you feel like it's not gonna happen,

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:33.303
you feel like he's not gonna say it,

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:35.883
don't go for it,

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:39.050
you could get in trouble.

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:42.090
I'm special council for internal affairs,

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:44.370
and I'm telling you you could
get in a lot of trouble.

00:22:44.370 --> 00:22:46.350
- Okay, they keep making an issue here

00:22:46.350 --> 00:22:49.380
that he can't go after Colonel Jessep

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.060
because it's illegal,

00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:53.910
it's attacking a superior officer,

00:22:53.910 --> 00:22:56.130
and something terrible is going to happen

00:22:56.130 --> 00:22:59.820
if he strenuously cross examines Jessep.

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:03.540
- After falsely accusing a
highly decorated Marine officer

00:23:03.540 --> 00:23:05.610
of conspiracy and perjury,

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.350
Lieutenant Kaffee will have a long

00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:11.580
and prosperous career teaching
type writer maintenance

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:14.220
at the Roccco Clubbo School for Women.

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:15.147
- Is that a thing?

00:23:15.147 --> 00:23:18.420
- No, no, I don't know what
the hell this was about.

00:23:18.420 --> 00:23:20.040
I think this is, as far as I can tell

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:22.431
some drama generation from Hollywood.

00:23:22.431 --> 00:23:26.010
If you have an adverse
witness on the stand,

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.990
you are allowed to question them.

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:29.880
- Probably ethically required to-

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:31.041
- Yes.

00:23:31.041 --> 00:23:31.874
- Go after them.
- Absolutely.

00:23:31.874 --> 00:23:34.740
- The defense calls Colonel Nathan Jessep.

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:37.410
Colonel, when you learned
of Santiago's letter

00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:41.730
to the NIS, you had a meeting
with your two senior officers,

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:42.630
is that right?

00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:43.590
- Yes.

00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:47.070
- At present Colonel Markinson
is dead, is that right?

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:47.903
- Objection.

00:23:47.903 --> 00:23:50.580
I'd like to know just what the
defense council is implying.

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:51.630
- Objection, I'd like to know

00:23:51.630 --> 00:23:53.822
what opposing council is doing.

00:23:53.822 --> 00:23:55.350
Not an objection.

00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:57.390
- No, just hey, can you give me

00:23:57.390 --> 00:23:59.040
your trial strategy up front please?

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.690
- I don't know what it is your honor,

00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:02.490
make him tell me.

00:24:02.490 --> 00:24:04.457
- Yeah, that's a little known fact

00:24:04.457 --> 00:24:06.420
of the uniform code of military justice,

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:09.569
you're required to trade
trial strategy memorandum.

00:24:09.569 --> 00:24:10.402
- Oh.

00:24:10.402 --> 00:24:11.790
- Yeah, I mean it's weird,

00:24:11.790 --> 00:24:13.110
but you know...

00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:14.100
- Colonel, at the time of this meeting

00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:16.530
you gave Kendrick an order, is that right?

00:24:16.530 --> 00:24:18.360
- I told Kendrick to tell his men

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:21.180
that Santiago wasn't to be touched.

00:24:21.180 --> 00:24:24.210
- And did you give an order
to Colonel Markinson as well?

00:24:24.210 --> 00:24:26.640
- I ordered Markinson to have Santiago

00:24:26.640 --> 00:24:29.520
transferred off the base immediately.

00:24:29.520 --> 00:24:30.353
- [Danny] Why?

00:24:31.410 --> 00:24:33.270
- I felt his life might be in danger

00:24:33.270 --> 00:24:35.580
once word of the letter got out.

00:24:35.580 --> 00:24:37.230
- Grave danger?

00:24:37.230 --> 00:24:39.281
- Is there another kind?

00:24:39.281 --> 00:24:40.830
(Devin and Spencer laughing)

00:24:40.830 --> 00:24:41.790
- It just occurred to me

00:24:41.790 --> 00:24:45.030
why I know the dialogue in
this scene particularly well.

00:24:45.030 --> 00:24:47.940
Obviously this is one of the
greatest courtroom scenes

00:24:47.940 --> 00:24:49.230
of all time,

00:24:49.230 --> 00:24:53.100
however, I know the
dialogue extremely well

00:24:53.100 --> 00:24:55.260
because when I was in high school

00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:56.820
I would do speech competitions

00:24:56.820 --> 00:24:59.880
and every year someone,

00:24:59.880 --> 00:25:02.250
the duo category with two people

00:25:02.250 --> 00:25:05.430
would do a recreation of
this cross examination,

00:25:05.430 --> 00:25:09.098
and so I heard this every weekend

00:25:09.098 --> 00:25:09.960
for years on end.

00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:11.490
- Was that the first flight off the base?

00:25:11.490 --> 00:25:15.420
- The 0600 was the first
flight off the base.

00:25:15.420 --> 00:25:16.920
- You flew out to Washington
early this morning,

00:25:16.920 --> 00:25:17.910
is that right?

00:25:17.910 --> 00:25:18.743
- Yes.

00:25:18.743 --> 00:25:20.610
- I notice you're wearing
your class A dress uniform

00:25:20.610 --> 00:25:21.960
for your appearance in court today.

00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:24.660
- No, he's not wearing
his class A dress uniform.

00:25:24.660 --> 00:25:27.690
Those are his service outfits.

00:25:27.690 --> 00:25:29.640
Thank you very much though, Mr. Navy Man.

00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:31.320
- Did you wear that uniform on the plane?

00:25:31.320 --> 00:25:33.090
- I wore utilities on the plane.

00:25:33.090 --> 00:25:35.430
- You brought your dress uniform with you?

00:25:35.430 --> 00:25:36.510
- Yes.

00:25:36.510 --> 00:25:39.180
- Toothbrush, a shaving
kit, change of underwear.

00:25:39.180 --> 00:25:40.013
- Your honor.

00:25:40.013 --> 00:25:41.756
- Is the Colonel's undewear a matter

00:25:41.756 --> 00:25:42.589
of national security?

00:25:42.589 --> 00:25:43.500
- Gentleman.

00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:45.810
You better get somewhere
fast with this lieutenant.

00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:46.643
- Yes, sir.

00:25:46.643 --> 00:25:47.476
Colonel.

00:25:47.476 --> 00:25:49.800
- He's so clearly laying a
foundation for something,

00:25:49.800 --> 00:25:51.780
come on, stop objecting,

00:25:51.780 --> 00:25:53.558
let him just get on with it.

00:25:53.558 --> 00:25:56.070
- Again, it's not like
this has been dragging on

00:25:56.070 --> 00:25:57.411
for 45 minutes.

00:25:57.411 --> 00:25:59.220
- Yeah, he's been on the
stand for like 30 seconds.

00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:00.270
- [Spencer] Yeah.

00:26:00.270 --> 00:26:02.040
- I brought a change of clothes

00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:03.843
and some personal items.

00:26:04.710 --> 00:26:05.820
- Thank you.

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:08.130
Santiago's barracks room was sealed off

00:26:08.130 --> 00:26:10.290
and its contents inventoried.

00:26:10.290 --> 00:26:11.970
Four pairs camouflage pants,

00:26:11.970 --> 00:26:13.470
three long sleeve kHaki shirts,

00:26:13.470 --> 00:26:14.511
three pairs of boots,

00:26:14.511 --> 00:26:16.200
four pairs green socks,

00:26:16.200 --> 00:26:17.580
three OD green t-shirts-

00:26:17.580 --> 00:26:18.930
- Please, the court, is there a question

00:26:18.930 --> 00:26:20.490
anywhere in our future?

00:26:20.490 --> 00:26:22.530
- I'm wondering why
Santiago wasn't packed.

00:26:22.530 --> 00:26:24.810
- A classic way of doing
exactly the same thing,

00:26:24.810 --> 00:26:26.700
but with even more power

00:26:26.700 --> 00:26:27.900
would be to lay the foundation

00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:28.920
for the document that he's reading.

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:31.283
Also, I don't think he's
entered that document

00:26:31.283 --> 00:26:32.116
into evidence.

00:26:32.116 --> 00:26:33.090
But let's assume he did.

00:26:33.090 --> 00:26:34.860
Giving it to the witness

00:26:34.860 --> 00:26:36.870
and say read this section.

00:26:36.870 --> 00:26:38.400
- You want the witness to be saying

00:26:38.400 --> 00:26:40.170
the words you want them to say.

00:26:40.170 --> 00:26:41.003
- Yep.

00:26:41.003 --> 00:26:42.064
Yeah, exactly.

00:26:42.064 --> 00:26:42.897
- Your honor, these are
the telephone records

00:26:42.897 --> 00:26:45.450
from Getmo for September 6th,

00:26:45.450 --> 00:26:47.880
and these are 14 letters

00:26:47.880 --> 00:26:50.610
that Santiago wrote in nine months

00:26:50.610 --> 00:26:53.190
requesting, in fact
begging for a transfer.

00:26:53.190 --> 00:26:54.780
- I guess it's not in evidence,

00:26:54.780 --> 00:26:57.065
we're just gonna have to
take your word for it.

00:26:57.065 --> 00:26:58.096
(Spencer laughing)

00:26:58.096 --> 00:26:59.700
- The fact is there was
no transfer ordered,

00:26:59.700 --> 00:27:02.520
Santiago wasn't going anywhere,
isn't that right, Colonel?

00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:04.219
- Objection, your honor,

00:27:04.219 --> 00:27:05.880
it's obvious Lieutenant Kaffee's
intention this afternoon

00:27:05.880 --> 00:27:08.070
was to smear a high ranking Marine officer

00:27:08.070 --> 00:27:09.120
in the desperate hope

00:27:09.120 --> 00:27:10.680
the mere appearance of impropriety

00:27:10.680 --> 00:27:12.180
will win him points
with the court members-

00:27:12.180 --> 00:27:14.310
- That is not an objection.

00:27:14.310 --> 00:27:15.210
It's a speaking objection,

00:27:15.210 --> 00:27:16.890
but it has no basis whatsoever,

00:27:16.890 --> 00:27:17.970
as far as I can tell.

00:27:17.970 --> 00:27:21.600
And also, you're telling the jury

00:27:21.600 --> 00:27:23.910
that he's scoring points
against your witness.

00:27:23.910 --> 00:27:26.670
This objection, this witness
is being torn to shreds

00:27:26.670 --> 00:27:28.620
your honor, we need to put a stop to it.

00:27:28.620 --> 00:27:30.180
No, stop it.

00:27:30.180 --> 00:27:31.770
- Now it's my recommendation, sir,

00:27:31.770 --> 00:27:34.230
that Lieutenant Kaffee be
reprimanded for his conduct,

00:27:34.230 --> 00:27:35.340
and the witness be excused

00:27:35.340 --> 00:27:37.200
with the court's deepest apologies.

00:27:37.200 --> 00:27:39.413
- The defendant's rights
not withstanding of course.

00:27:39.413 --> 00:27:40.612
(Devin laughing)

00:27:40.612 --> 00:27:44.460
- And let's just execute
the defendants your honor.

00:27:44.460 --> 00:27:46.020
I've had enough of this trial

00:27:46.020 --> 00:27:47.580
and due process.

00:27:47.580 --> 00:27:48.990
- Lieutenant Kendrick
ordered the code red,

00:27:48.990 --> 00:27:50.172
didn't he?

00:27:50.172 --> 00:27:51.420
Because that's what you told
Lieutenant Kendrick to do.

00:27:51.420 --> 00:27:52.253
- Object-

00:27:52.253 --> 00:27:54.287
- And when it went bad
you cut these guys loose.

00:27:54.287 --> 00:27:55.192
- Your honor.

00:27:55.192 --> 00:27:57.180
- You had Markinson sign
a phony transfer letter.

00:27:57.180 --> 00:27:58.710
You doctored the log book.

00:27:58.710 --> 00:28:00.480
- Yeah, and now we're badgering

00:28:00.480 --> 00:28:01.881
and being argumentative.

00:28:01.881 --> 00:28:03.777
- Did you order the code red?

00:28:03.777 --> 00:28:05.550
- You don't have to answer that question.

00:28:05.550 --> 00:28:07.710
- I'll answer the question.

00:28:07.710 --> 00:28:08.820
You want answers?

00:28:08.820 --> 00:28:09.780
- I think I'm entitled.

00:28:09.780 --> 00:28:11.220
- [Nathan] You want answers.

00:28:11.220 --> 00:28:12.180
- I want the truth.

00:28:12.180 --> 00:28:14.490
- You can't handle the truth.

00:28:14.490 --> 00:28:15.323
You don't want the truth,

00:28:15.323 --> 00:28:18.520
because deep down in places
you don't talk about at parties

00:28:19.718 --> 00:28:20.760
you want me on that wall.

00:28:20.760 --> 00:28:22.830
You need me on that wall.

00:28:22.830 --> 00:28:24.120
- The fence at Guantanamo

00:28:24.120 --> 00:28:27.180
is probably a really sleepy place.

00:28:27.180 --> 00:28:30.240
- Yeah, about as sleepy as
a posting as you can get.

00:28:30.240 --> 00:28:32.130
I mean, imagine that he was

00:28:32.130 --> 00:28:34.410
a Marine Security Guard Commander

00:28:34.410 --> 00:28:37.080
at one of these nuclear bases in Seattle

00:28:37.080 --> 00:28:38.580
or something like that.

00:28:38.580 --> 00:28:40.110
Using this exact same language-

00:28:40.110 --> 00:28:42.720
- You want me on that chain link fence.

00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:43.553
- That's right.

00:28:43.553 --> 00:28:46.050
- You need me in front of
that nuclear power plant.

00:28:46.050 --> 00:28:46.883
- Don't get me wrong,

00:28:46.883 --> 00:28:47.853
it's important work,

00:28:48.753 --> 00:28:49.586
it needs to be done,

00:28:49.586 --> 00:28:51.780
but the stakes are not this high.

00:28:51.780 --> 00:28:53.460
- Deep down inside

00:28:53.460 --> 00:28:57.347
you need me to guard the 7-Eleven.

00:28:57.347 --> 00:29:02.008
- I don't give a damn what
you think you are entitled to.

00:29:02.008 --> 00:29:03.254
- Did you order the code red?

00:29:03.254 --> 00:29:04.765
- I don't care, I don't
care, it's awesome.

00:29:04.765 --> 00:29:05.598
- Did you order the code red?

00:29:05.598 --> 00:29:07.350
- You're goddamn right I did.

00:29:07.350 --> 00:29:08.310
- Yes.

00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:10.530
We both know you can't shout in court.

00:29:10.530 --> 00:29:12.060
The witnesses aren't gonna shout.

00:29:12.060 --> 00:29:14.220
The lawyers aren't gonna shout.

00:29:14.220 --> 00:29:15.840
But it's so good.

00:29:15.840 --> 00:29:16.746
- It's so good.

00:29:16.746 --> 00:29:17.700
- It's so good.

00:29:17.700 --> 00:29:20.340
- There's a reason why this is a classic,

00:29:20.340 --> 00:29:21.660
and it's that.

00:29:21.660 --> 00:29:23.370
- Jack Nicholson is in this movie

00:29:23.370 --> 00:29:25.056
for five minutes.

